In the crystal chamber
A round chamber with crystal walls, floor and a domed ceiling. A short black tube-like console stands to one side next to a pit in the centre of the room. On the wall opposite a wheel and a lever are seen next to each other. The most remarkable thing is the large red crystal rod hanging mysteriously without support centrally above the pit. You have no idea what this place was used for but it looks important.
You can go down.
You can see a console (on which there is a red button, a yellow button, a green button and a blue button), a wheel, a lever, a rod, a dome, a pit and a recess.
> pull lever

You pull the lever and the pit opens.
> put cask of gunpowder in pit

Done.

Your creator Viktor Frankenstein walks into the chamber and pleads for you to return home with him.
> push yellow button

You hear a loud ping. It's the correct button sequence.
> push green button

You hear a loud ping. It's the correct button sequence.
> push blue button

You hear a loud ping. It's the correct button sequence.
> push red button

You hear a loud ping. It's the correct button sequence and the rod starts pulsating giving off a strong glow. A beam of red light shoots down into the pit. The pit acts like a battery and charges up the city's power.
The beam of light heats up the cask of gunpowder!

Frankenstein leaps into action and pushes you out of the way of the blast. Unfortunately, he takes the full force of it and is ripped asunder scattering bodies parts all over the chamber. As you stare at your creator's remains you speak.

"I shall die, and what I now feel be no longer felt. Soon these burning miseries will be extinct. I shall ascend my funeral pile triumphantly and exult in the agony of the torturing flames. The light of that conflagration will fade away; my ashes will be swept into the sea by the winds. My spirit will sleep in peace, or if it thinks, it will not surely think thus. Farewell."

The End
